A||||6||shark93726||Steering ratios for Fieros?||||1||
Z||000000||shark93726||11-24-2001||01:57 PM||||Can anyone tell me if any year Fieros have quicker steering ratio <BR>than others, and if so, which years or models have the quickest ratio.<P>Or, are there any aftermarket rack and pinions with quicker ratio?<P>I have an '87 and am building a lightweight '84 for autocrossing, so <BR>the quicker the better.<P>Thanks in advance,<P>Gerald Storvik (8shark.com)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||11-24-2001||03:16 PM||||Fiero's are 19:1 steering ratio. IRM use to sell a 16:1 rack. I don't know if they still sell them or not. It was the same one used on the REAL Pace cars. They use to sell them for $450. I'm not sure if you can modify a stock one with different gears to get the ratio better.||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||11-24-2001||04:34 PM||||From all my testing, there's two of them.  And they're damn close.  <P>The V6 cars got a ~3.25 lock to lock and the 4cyl's got a ~3.5 lock to lock.  Not to say that that's gospil or anything...  just what I've found myself.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||11-24-2001||09:25 PM||||According to Autozone and Advance Auto parts books, there are two available for 84-87.  My 86 GT gets a quicker (16:1) ratio than a standard Fiero (19:1).  Same price for either at Autozone (around $140 last time I checked), but almost $400 for the 16:1 at Advance.  All rebuilt stuff, too.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||11-24-2001||09:39 PM||||I <I>think</I> -- although I can't prove it -- that '84-'87 cars with WS6 suspension/steering option have a faster steering rack, something like 3 turns lock-to-lock <I>vs.</I> 3-1/2 turns standard.  Also, somewhere I have read that IMSA Fieros had 2- or 2-1/2-turn racks.  Good luck finding one!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||11-25-2001||02:16 AM||||According to my Gary Witzenburg Fiero book (just dug it out), page 118, 19.2:1 for all 84's, 85-88 GT, and 88 coupe.  formulas's not specifically included in the chart, but a good bet.<P>85-87 coupe, sport coupe, and SE all had 22:1.<P>That's according to the book.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Posthumane||11-25-2001||02:24 AM||||I have an 84 SE with the WS6 handling package, and it has 3 turns lock to lock. Not sure what the ratio is, but the turn radius is huge for a car this size.||||reg||1
